    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "i don't know if rest is even an option anymore. it feels less like \"burnout\" and more like a terminal error. if the output is always going to be zero, the cost of staying in the system just keeps rising. i look at the projection for the next ten years and it's just... empty. so when you talk about \"finding momentum again,\" it sounds like asking someone to keep running a program that has already crashed. if the system is fundamentally broken, isn't it more logical to just shut it down than to keep consuming resources?",
